Aim
To write a simple Java program that uses Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum possible profit from a given array of daily profit and loss values. Essentially, this will identify the subarray (a continuous sequence of days) that results in the highest profit.
program:
public class MaxProfitKadane {

    // Function to apply Kadane's Algorithm
    public static int maxProfit(int[] dailyChanges) {
        int maxSoFar = dailyChanges[0];
        int maxEndingHere = dailyChanges[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < dailyChanges.length; i++) {
            maxEndingHere = Math.max(dailyChanges[i], maxEndingHere + dailyChanges[i]);
            maxSoFar = Math.max(maxSoFar, maxEndingHere);
        }
        return maxSoFar;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Example daily profit and loss values
        int[] dailyChanges = { -2, 3, -1, 2, -1, 2, -3, 4 };

        System.out.println("Daily profit/loss values:");
        for (int val : dailyChanges) {
            System.out.print(val + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();

        int maxProfit = maxProfit(dailyChanges);
        System.out.println("Maximum possible profit: " + maxProfit);
    }
}

